apbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bd0b9d8ef68d70163ca0996ef792164530869dabb07ddeb2df41922259b62470","event_uuid":"741eea45-0696-4639-a779-ff51e8ef6db6","position":{"commit_sha":"00d2ff2fbddff610ecceea963fab70d983607caa","position":"1786588838064722801-741eea45-0696-4639-a779-ff51e8ef6db6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree arcticseal-cap-warning (base f20e053aad).\n\nCorrection recorded: AC1 was already satisfied on main by 7cf80009d9 — the cap is the pre-existing config key verify.max_ticket_description_chars (default 8000), read by the plan-review guard (det_floor P4) and the completion precheck. This change adds a THIRD reader rather than a new key, preserving single-sourcing.\n\nDesign: gates.description_cap_warning() computes the notice, reusing _plan_review_gate_applies() — the exact probe the claim path uses — so the warning cannot promise a block the gate would not make. It is computed AFTER the CREATE/EDIT event is appended and degrades to None on any error, so it can never block or alter a write.\n\nChannels per surface: CLI prints 'Warning: …' to stderr (stdout stays pure in text and json modes, exit code 0); the library logs it on the rebar logger (edit_ticket now returns it, create_ticket(return_alias=True) carries description_warning); MCP returns a description_warning result field on CreateResultOut/WriteAckOut, mirroring push_status.\n\nGates: make lint, make typecheck, module-size (800) and the locked complexity ratchet all pass. The ratchet forced two extractions (_warn_stderr, _edit_description_warning) rather than raising locked ceilings, and _lib_writes.py was trimmed to exactly the 800-line cap. 22 new tests in tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py; a mutation probe (forcing the helper to return None) kills 9 of them across all three surfaces.","timestamp":1786585557352294001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed for review as Gerrit change 1697 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1697), commit 5219f06f96 on base f20e053aad.\n\nFull suite before push: 12528 passed, 52 skipped, 1 error. The single error was a teardown repo-root-leak guard on test_repair_snapshots_dry_run_writes_nothing — a test this change does not touch; it passes clean in isolation (2 passed) and was caused by two suite runs briefly overlapping on this host, not by the change.","timestamp":1786588362324307001}],"created_at":1786583255968576001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"741eea45-0696-4639-a779-ff51e8ef6db6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f587-e586-1f39-47b0"}],"description":"## Context\nOperator-specified (2026-08-12, verbatim): \"The 8k cap should be pulling from a config key, defaulting to 8k. When a ticket is saved with a description over the configured cap (create or edit) and the plan review gate is enabled for the project (claim will fail without a passing review), we should display a warning at the time of save to give the client a heads-up that they'll need to edit the description. This provides a more immediate feedback loop instead of waiting for someone to try to run plan review.\"\n\nBackground: the plan-review admission guard (landed as 7cf80009d9) fast-fails reviews on descriptions over the limit. Tonight FOUR agents hit it blind at review time (8,001 / 8,001 / 8,180 / three children at 11k-22k) - the late feedback loop is measured waste.\n\n## Correction to AC1 (recorded after code inspection)\nAC1 is ALREADY SATISFIED on main by 7cf80009d9: the cap is the config key\n`verify.max_ticket_description_chars` (default 8000, `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`),\nread by the review guard (`llm/plan_review/det_floor.py::_description_limit`, P4) and by\nthe completion precheck (`llm/workflow/gate_ops.py`). No NEW key is introduced; the\nsave-time warning becomes a THIRD reader of that same key, preserving single-sourcing.\nScope of this ticket is therefore AC2-AC5 plus a test pinning the shared source.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py` (242 LOC, the single home of gate enablement) - add\n   `description_cap_warning(description, ticket_type, *, ticket_id, repo_root) -> str | None`.\n   It loads config once for `verify.max_ticket_description_chars`, returns None when the\n   description is within the cap, and otherwise reuses the CLAIM path's existing probe\n   `_plan_review_gate_applies()` (which wraps `gate_enabled(\"require_plan_review_for_claim\")`\n   and the `_PLAN_REVIEW_EXEMPT_TYPES` tuple) - no new probe invented. Returns None when\n   the gate is off/exempt. Message states actual length, the cap, and that claim requires a\n   passing plan review which refuses admission until the description is shortened. It never\n   raises: any unexpected error returns None (the warning must never affect the write).\n\n2. `src/rebar/_commands/composer.py` - compute the warning AFTER the CREATE/EDIT event is\n   appended (so the write is never altered or blocked) and return it:\n   - `create_core` adds `\"description_warning\"` to its returned dict.\n   - `edit_core` returns `str | None` instead of None (only when a description field was\n     written); ticket type is read from compiled state / the edited `ticket_type` field.\n   - `create_cli` / `edit_cli` print `Warning: <msg>` to **stderr** (the established CLI\n     channel, mirroring the existing no-file_impact nudge in `create_cli`), stdout stays\n     pure in both text and json modes, exit code stays 0.\n\n3. `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` - `create_ticket` and `edit_ticket` emit the warning through\n   the **rebar logger** (`logging.getLogger(__name__).warning`), the documented library\n   channel (`_logging.py`; the `rebar` root carries a NullHandler, so an embedding caller\n   opts in, and the CLI/MCP stderr handlers show it). `edit_ticket`'s return type widens\n   from `None` to `str | None` (additive: None when there is no warning) so a programmatic\n   caller can surface it - the same reasoning already documented on `link()`.\n   `create_ticket(return_alias=True)` carries `description_warning` in its dict.\n\n4. `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` + `_mcp_models.py` - surface it as a RESULT FIELD, exactly the\n   `push_status` precedent (an MCP client reads only the tool result): add optional\n   `description_warning: str | None = None` to `CreateResultOut` and `WriteAckOut` (both\n   already `extra=\"allow\"`, so this is a strict superset of today's shape), thread it from\n   `create_ticket` and `edit_ticket`.\n\n5. `docs/config.md` - extend the existing `verify.max_ticket_description_chars` entry to\n   record that create/edit warn at save time when the value is exceeded and the claim gate\n   is on. No new key, so no env-registry regeneration.\n\n## Testing\nProving command: `pytest tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py tests/unit/test_ticket_description_limit.py -q`, plus `make lint` and `make typecheck`. New tests in `tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py`:\n- over-cap + gate ON warns, on create and on edit, per surface: CLI stderr (capsys), library\n  logger (caplog), MCP result field.\n- over-cap + gate OFF: silent on all three.\n- under-cap (and exactly at the cap - 8000 allowed, 8001 warns): silent.\n- exempt ticket type (bug) with gate on: silent.\n- config key respected: a non-default `verify.max_ticket_description_chars` moves the\n  threshold, and the default is 8000; a test pins that the warning and the review guard\n  read the SAME key.\n- the write still succeeds and is unaltered when warning (ticket description round-trips).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1 - The admission cap reads from a config key defaulting to 8000, and the review guard and the new save-time warning read the SAME key (single source). (Key pre-exists: `verify.max_ticket_description_chars`.)\n- [ ] AC2 - On `create` and `edit` (CLI, library, MCP), when the saved description exceeds the configured cap AND the plan-review claim gate is enabled, a warning is emitted at save time stating the length, the cap, and that claim will require a passing review which refuses admission until the description is shortened. The save still succeeds.\n- [ ] AC3 - No warning when the gate is disabled, or when the description is within the cap; the warning never blocks or alters the write.\n- [ ] AC4 - Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py`: tests cover: over-cap+gate-on warns (create and edit, each surface's channel - CLI stderr, library logger, MCP result field); over-cap+gate-off silent; under-cap silent; config key respected and default correct.\n- [ ] AC5 - docs/config.md documents the save-time warning; verified by `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `pytest tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py tests/unit/test_ticket_description_limit.py`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/gates.py","reason":"new description_cap_warning helper reusing the claim gate probe"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"create_core/edit_core compute+return the warning; create_cli/edit_cli print it to stderr"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"library channel: logger.warning on create/edit; edit_ticket returns the warning"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"thread the warning into MCP tool results"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"optional description_warning field on CreateResultOut/WriteAckOut"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document the save-time warning on the existing cap key"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py","reason":"new tests for all three surfaces, gate on/off, cap boundary"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","f587-e586-1f39-47b0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c283dfab-8adb-41ce-8704-2c2e56d12a2a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"594b-3118-208c-4766","ticket_type":"task","title":"Config-driven description cap with save-time warning","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f285474a-9139-4910-aaa8-622adb07f71d","5795b371-9d45-4a27-866b-4e2efbeb9794","c2748678-f794-4934-bb77-fbe2ffc3e6d6","6fc6d295-b4a3-41bc-915a-711a5ef46084","2b2fedec-0ac0-4a99-9bff-36471f279fe1","c283dfab-8adb-41ce-8704-2c2e56d12a2a","56056315-88af-4d62-a128-a79f2791f7b8","a0352916-76c2-42bf-8463-217329566c28","192c8772-a137-4292-8140-830eaaf66cc7","741eea45-0696-4639-a779-ff51e8ef6db6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786588838064722802,"uuid":"0ddc3c0e-2988-4a8c-be16-507c091d838e"}